# What this desktop opens a folder with, and only while this desktop is the one
# running: the file that names it is read by anything following the mime-apps
# specification, and only when `XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP` lowercases to the name in
# front of `-mimeapps.list`. LineXinBar's session sets it (see
# packaging/files/lxb-session), so a LineXinBar session gets Files and a KDE
# session on the same machine keeps Dolphin — without either of them writing to
# the user's own `mimeapps.list`.
#
# Only `[Default Applications]` belongs here. A desktop-specific list may not
# add or remove associations, and GLib says so out loud when one tries; what
# Files can open is on the entry itself.
[Default Applications]
inode/directory=linexinbar-files.desktop
